{
  "answer_text": "The papers compare various methods and system variants, primarily categorized by their use of external knowledge, training adjustments, and decoding strategies. The specific conditions compared across the studies include:\n\n1. **Parametric-Only / Closed-Book / No-Retrieval Baseline:** Models that answer using only internal parametric knowledge without accessing external documents [S001, 1034-1471], [S003, 1430-1801], [S004, 1336-1583], [S005, 1084-1523], [S006, 1378-2114], [S007, 1438-1856], [S008, 971-1564], [S009, 1281-1620], [S010, 1159-1430], [S011, 1097-1529], [S012, 1357-1649], [S013, 1327-1715], [S014, 919-1194], [S015, 1305-1704], [S016, 1406-2238], [S017, 1515-1969], [S018, 1198-1455], [S019, 1167-1444], [S020, 1513-1892].\n\n2. **Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) / Retrieve-Then-Read:** Systems that retrieve relevant passages from a reference collection and condition their answers on them [S001, 1034-1471], [S002, 1171-1699], [S003, 1430-1801], [S004, 1336-1583], [S005, 1084-1523], [S006, 1378-2114], [S007, 1438-1856], [S008, 971-1564], [S009, 1281-1620], [S010, 1159-1430], [S011, 1097-1529], [S012, 1357-1649], [S013, 1327-1715], [S014, 919-1194], [S015, 1305-1704], [S016, 1406-2238], [S017, 1515-1969], [S018, 1198-1455], [S019, 1167-1444], [S020, 1513-1892].\n\n3. **Fine-Tuned Models:** Models that undergo additional training on in-domain question and answer pairs [S001, 1034-1471], [S005, 1084-1523], [S006, 1378-2114], [S007, 1438-1856], [S015, 1305-1704], [S017, 1515-1969], [S019, 1167-1444], [S020, 1513-1892].\n\n4. **Chain-of-Thought (CoT) Prompting:** Conditions where the model is asked to write out its reasoning before providing the final answer [S001, 1034-1471], [S011, 1097-1529].\n\n5. **RAG Variants:**\n   - **RAG without Reranking:** Uses the same retriever but keeps passages in their original order [S002, 1171-1699], [S005, 1084-1523], [S010, 1159-1430].\n   - **RAG with Random Passages:** Receives passages drawn at random from the collection instead of retrieved ones [S011, 1097-1529], [S013, 1327-1715], [S015, 1305-1704], [S016, 1406-2238].\n   - **Query Rewriting/Reformulation:** Rewrites the question into a search query before consulting the collection [S002, 1171-1699], [S016, 1406-2238].\n\n6. **Self-Consistency / Voting:** Models that sample several answers and return the most frequent one [S017, 1515-1969], [S020, 1513-1892].",
